1
00:00:03,303 --> 00:00:05,304
JACK: Torchwood.

2
00:00:05,406 --> 00:00:08,207
Outside the government,
beyond the police.

3
00:00:08,308 --> 00:00:11,644
Fighting for the future
on behalf of the human race.

4
00:00:12,446 --> 00:00:15,481
The 2 1 st century
is when everything changes

5
00:00:15,582 --> 00:00:17,550
and Torchwood is ready.

6
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:42,909
Gwen, texting you the location.

7
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:46,212
Appearing four or five signs of life.
Definitely non-human.

8
00:00:46,313 --> 00:00:48,681
-Get here as soon as you can.
-So, sure they're not Weevils?

9
00:00:48,782 --> 00:00:51,517
Don't think so.
Different energy patterns.

10
00:00:51,618 --> 00:00:53,553
Can't make sense of it.

11
00:00:53,654 --> 00:00:57,123
-Not a species we've encountered before.
-Let's hope they're friendly, then.

12
00:00:57,224 --> 00:00:59,726
Owen, Ianto, take the other side
of the building. Check the upper floors.

13
00:00:59,827 --> 00:01:01,461
Toshiko, with me.

14
00:01:07,501 --> 00:01:08,601
Okay?

15
00:01:09,603 --> 00:01:10,670
Go.

16
00:01:18,412 --> 00:01:21,280
I'm getting mirror readings
on both floors.

17
00:01:22,382 --> 00:01:25,218
One creature at either end
of the building.

18
00:01:25,853 --> 00:01:28,287
Toshiko, split up.

19
00:01:37,765 --> 00:01:40,533
You know,
these creatures are very quiet.

20
00:01:41,401 --> 00:01:43,336
Maybe they're sleeping.

21
00:01:44,271 --> 00:01:45,938
Or hatching.

22
00:01:51,145 --> 00:01:53,780
Or maybe they aren't creatures at all.

23
00:01:58,652 --> 00:02:00,620
Just explosive devices.

24
00:02:04,258 --> 00:02:05,358
Snap.

25
00:02:23,043 --> 00:02:24,477
(RINGING)

26
00:02:27,447 --> 00:02:28,581
Shit!

27
00:02:33,287 --> 00:02:37,190
-You have one message.
-IANTO: Gwen, texting you the location.

28
00:02:37,291 --> 00:02:40,126
-Appearing four or five signs of life.
-Shit!

29
00:03:00,647 --> 00:03:02,181
(GASPING)

30
00:03:03,717 --> 00:03:05,051
Not again.

31
00:03:13,894 --> 00:03:15,361
(GRU NTING)

32
00:03:23,804 --> 00:03:25,004
Ladies!

33
00:03:26,406 --> 00:03:30,643
Torso of steel, shilling a feel.
Any takers?

34
00:03:31,612 --> 00:03:32,979
(GRU NTING)

35
00:03:34,248 --> 00:03:37,583
Bar fight, got a little out of control.
Flesh wound.

36
00:03:39,386 --> 00:03:41,320
Oh ! Still not used to...

37
00:03:43,423 --> 00:03:45,024
These hangovers.

38
00:03:47,327 --> 00:03:50,496
Captain Jack Harkness.
How long have you been there?

39
00:03:50,597 --> 00:03:54,934
Silent types? That's okay.
I used to date a guy with no mouth.

40
00:03:55,535 --> 00:03:57,003
Surprisingly creative.

41
00:04:00,841 --> 00:04:03,175
Now listen, you only had to ask.

42
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:05,611
Can we get a room, though?

43
00:04:07,514 --> 00:04:08,981
(COUGHING)

44
00:04:14,354 --> 00:04:15,721
(SCREAMING)

45
00:04:19,526 --> 00:04:23,462
When I said about getting a room,
I meant somewhere with linen.

46
00:04:24,197 --> 00:04:25,564
(SCREAMING)

47
00:04:28,702 --> 00:04:32,972
Time was electrodes to the nipples
meant the start of a good night.

48
00:04:34,007 --> 00:04:35,641
(JACK SCREAMING)

49
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:44,850
(JACK LAUGHING)

50
00:04:45,652 --> 00:04:48,254
Full power charge and still breathing.

51
00:04:48,355 --> 00:04:50,556
Pretty advanced piece of equipment
you got there.

52
00:04:50,657 --> 00:04:54,694
You ladies are ahead of yourselves.
Now where the hell am I?

53
00:04:57,497 --> 00:04:58,731
Put that down before someone gets...

54
00:05:00,901 --> 00:05:02,168
(GASPING)

55
00:05:03,937 --> 00:05:05,171
Why aren't you dead yet?

56
00:05:05,272 --> 00:05:08,040
-Been trying to figure that out myself.
-We've been monitoring you.

57
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:11,410
You've been killed 14 times
in the last 6 months.

58
00:05:11,511 --> 00:05:13,679
-Feels like more than that.
-Who's the Doctor?

59
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:15,214
No idea.

60
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:17,850
"The Doctor. He will be able to fix me."

61
00:05:17,951 --> 00:05:21,153
"When the Doctor turns up,
it'll all be put right."

62
00:05:21,254 --> 00:05:23,289
"You wait till I see the Doctor."

63
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:26,760
" First I'm going to kiss him,
then I'm going to kill him."

64
00:05:26,974 --> 00:05:30,176
-Why do you want to know?
-You're in Torchwood, Cardiff.

65
00:05:30,277 --> 00:05:35,448
The Torchwood Institute was created
to combat the threat posed by the Doctor

66
00:05:35,549 --> 00:05:37,550
and other phantasmagoria.

67
00:05:39,854 --> 00:05:41,354
JACK: He's not a threat!

68
00:05:41,455 --> 00:05:45,892
The Doctor is the one who will save you
from your phantasma-hoogits.

69
00:05:45,993 --> 00:05:48,795
-Just tell us his location.
-I don't know!

70
00:05:52,166 --> 00:05:55,602
He left me behind.
I came here to find him.

71
00:05:57,338 --> 00:06:01,174
He refuels from that rift you have.

72
00:06:01,275 --> 00:06:04,911
Hoping if I stayed here long enough,
we'd find each other.

73
00:06:06,447 --> 00:06:07,514
Now...

74
00:06:08,616 --> 00:06:10,583
-Can I go?
-No.

75
00:06:10,684 --> 00:06:12,986
-You can't keep me here.
-We can.

76
00:06:13,888 --> 00:06:16,990
-Unless.
-Yes. Unless...

77
00:06:17,091 --> 00:06:18,425
Unless what?

78
00:06:18,526 --> 00:06:21,428
There are opportunities here
with the Institute.

79
00:06:21,529 --> 00:06:24,731
-I'm not for hire.
-You're going to need currency.

80
00:06:28,636 --> 00:06:30,503
-What's the assignment?
-Missing person.

81
00:06:30,604 --> 00:06:32,672
Well, when we say person...

82
00:06:35,709 --> 00:06:37,210
I haven't done anything.

83
00:06:37,311 --> 00:06:39,612
12 burglaries,
joyriding a horse and carriage,

84
00:06:39,713 --> 00:06:41,181
seven cases of pickpocketing,

85
00:06:41,282 --> 00:06:44,017
24 instances of consuming food
without paying for it.

86
00:06:44,118 --> 00:06:45,819
It's like an addiction
with your species, isn't it?

87
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,455
I'll make it up, I promise.

88
00:06:48,556 --> 00:06:51,224
-Ohh. Too late.
-It's just a bit of fun.

89
00:06:51,358 --> 00:06:55,228
This planet's a century away from
official first contact with alien life.

90
00:06:55,329 --> 00:06:58,465
-You're upsetting the schedule.
-Who are you?

91
00:07:00,134 --> 00:07:01,601
I'm Torchwood.

92
00:07:03,270 --> 00:07:05,772
I said sorry! You can't lock me up.

93
00:07:05,873 --> 00:07:07,907
He's just a kid.
Send him back to where he came from.

94
00:07:08,008 --> 00:07:10,410
If only we could.
The rift only goes one way.

95
00:07:10,511 --> 00:07:12,312
What do you do?
Observe and profile the species,

96
00:07:12,413 --> 00:07:15,081
then transfer them to long-term storage?

97
00:07:18,519 --> 00:07:20,453
-Why!
-He was a threat to the Empire.

98
00:07:20,554 --> 00:07:23,556
-Like me?
-You're our ally now.

99
00:07:38,239 --> 00:07:40,173
If you don't want it...

100
00:07:46,914 --> 00:07:49,382
-Your next assignment.
- (SCOFFS) No.

101
00:07:50,184 --> 00:07:53,653
-I'm through with you people.
-Your liberty is at our discretion.

102
00:07:53,754 --> 00:07:58,625
Work for us, you assist the Empire.
Sever that tie, you become a threat.

103
00:07:59,093 --> 00:08:00,727
And you've seen
how we deal with threats.

104
00:08:00,828 --> 00:08:04,430
It's good money, Captain.
How else are you going to earn?

105
00:08:08,269 --> 00:08:09,869
(JACK SIGHING)

106
00:08:19,213 --> 00:08:21,648
See what you think in the morning.

107
00:08:27,188 --> 00:08:30,790
He's pretty. But you're prettier.

108
00:08:47,274 --> 00:08:49,108
Can I read your cards?

109
00:08:50,244 --> 00:08:51,711
No, thank you.

110
00:08:55,883 --> 00:08:57,250
No, really.

111
00:09:07,995 --> 00:09:10,763
He's coming, the one you're looking for.

112
00:09:17,605 --> 00:09:21,074
The century will turn twice
before you find each other.

113
00:09:22,243 --> 00:09:24,110
Ooh. Are you for real?

114
00:09:28,082 --> 00:09:31,417
You mean I have to wait
a hundred years to find him?

115
00:09:31,518 --> 00:09:32,752
(SCOFFS)

116
00:09:34,221 --> 00:09:36,422
What'll I do in the meantime?

117
00:10:28,575 --> 00:10:32,378
REPORTER: ...some parts of the world
have already welcomed in the new year.

118
00:10:32,479 --> 00:10:34,981
And our cameras,
of course, have been out in force

119
00:10:35,082 --> 00:10:38,818
across the U K tonight.
Let's take you first to Cardiff.

120
00:10:41,922 --> 00:10:44,857
Hey! When you joked about
the millennium bug,

121
00:10:44,958 --> 00:10:48,695
I didn't realise it was going
to have 18 legs stacked with poison.

122
00:10:48,796 --> 00:10:49,962
Anyone home?

123
00:10:50,064 --> 00:10:53,333
Hey, you know you're supposed to
party like it's...

124
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:14,253
Alex.

125
00:11:14,355 --> 00:11:16,823
Jack. Just in time.

126
00:11:18,826 --> 00:11:19,959
Alex?

127
00:11:20,394 --> 00:11:23,262
-What happened? Who did this?
-Me.

128
00:11:24,431 --> 00:11:25,531
What?

129
00:11:28,736 --> 00:11:30,403
Why?

130
00:11:30,504 --> 00:11:32,638
We got it wrong, Jack.

131
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:35,141
We thought we could control
the stuff we found.

132
00:11:35,242 --> 00:11:38,211
And what's it brought us? So much death.

133
00:11:39,813 --> 00:11:42,882
-What happened to them?
-It's good you're here.

134
00:11:44,284 --> 00:11:46,452
Always did have great timing.

135
00:11:47,187 --> 00:11:49,989
This place, it's yours.

136
00:11:50,858 --> 00:11:52,458
Torchwood Three.

137
00:11:53,394 --> 00:11:57,096
My gift to you, Jack, for a
century of service as field operative.

138
00:11:57,197 --> 00:11:59,365
Fill this place with purpose.

139
00:11:59,466 --> 00:12:01,834
Before it's too late. Please.

140
00:12:02,236 --> 00:12:03,669
Alex, listen.

141
00:12:04,638 --> 00:12:06,839
-It's going to be okay.
-No.

142
00:12:06,907 --> 00:12:08,174
It's not.

143
00:12:09,042 --> 00:12:10,610
It's really not.

144
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:14,480
I looked inside.

145
00:12:16,650 --> 00:12:18,751
It showed me what's coming.

146
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:21,821
They were mercy killings.

147
00:12:23,157 --> 00:12:26,125
It's the kindest thing I could do.

148
00:12:26,226 --> 00:12:28,361
So none of us see the storm.

149
00:12:28,462 --> 00:12:30,296
(CH EERING ON TV)

150
00:12:30,397 --> 00:12:33,032
I'm sorry I can't do the same for you.

151
00:12:35,969 --> 00:12:39,138
2 1 st century, Jack.
Everything's going to change.

152
00:12:40,941 --> 00:12:42,708
(CH EERING ON TV)

153
00:12:42,810 --> 00:12:45,478
-And we're not ready.
-Alex!

154
00:12:45,546 --> 00:12:47,079
(GU NSHOT)

155
00:12:50,717 --> 00:12:52,218
(GASPING)

156
00:12:52,319 --> 00:12:54,320
(JACK SCREAMING)

157
00:12:54,421 --> 00:12:56,923
He was dead !
I checked his pulse. He was dead !

158
00:12:57,024 --> 00:12:58,925
All right. Shh !

159
00:12:59,026 --> 00:13:01,227
Jack, what's happened?
Where are the others?

160
00:13:01,328 --> 00:13:03,796
-What is he doing here?
-I was late. He give me a lift.

161
00:13:03,897 --> 00:13:05,832
-You okay?
-Yeah. Yeah.

162
00:13:05,933 --> 00:13:08,267
Toshiko, she went the other way.

163
00:13:09,036 --> 00:13:11,337
(JACK SHOUTING IN TH E DISTANCE)

164
00:13:16,977 --> 00:13:21,714
GWEN : Toshiko, yell if you can hear me!
JACK: Toshiko! Toshiko!

165
00:13:23,450 --> 00:13:25,184
(PANTING)

166
00:13:31,391 --> 00:13:32,758
(SCREAMING)

167
00:13:39,933 --> 00:13:41,734
(KEYBOARD CLICKING)

168
00:13:44,838 --> 00:13:47,206
Never thought I'd say this
to anyone here,

169
00:13:47,307 --> 00:13:49,375
but you work too hard.

170
00:13:49,476 --> 00:13:51,310
Another hour and I'm done.

171
00:13:51,411 --> 00:13:53,212
I wish the rest of them
thought like you.

172
00:13:53,313 --> 00:13:56,148
At 5: 30, they're out of here
like a pack of dogs.

173
00:13:56,250 --> 00:13:59,085
-You have a good evening, sir.
-I doubt it.

174
00:16:23,697 --> 00:16:25,731
Another late one, Miss Sato?

175
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:28,701
You know me, George, married to the job.

176
00:16:28,802 --> 00:16:30,936
When are you going to let me
whisk you away from all this?

177
00:16:31,038 --> 00:16:33,506
As soon as you clear it
with your wife and grandchildren.

178
00:16:33,607 --> 00:16:37,610
-Always an excuse. Take care.
-Good night, George.

179
00:17:54,621 --> 00:17:56,322
-I've got it.
-Get in.

180
00:18:00,227 --> 00:18:01,627
(BEEPING)

181
00:18:06,032 --> 00:18:09,435
I want to see my mother.
I want to know she's safe.

182
00:18:09,503 --> 00:18:10,603
Now.

183
00:18:12,439 --> 00:18:14,106
Show me the piece.

184
00:18:22,182 --> 00:18:25,251
It's beautiful.
A perfect sonic modulator.

185
00:18:25,352 --> 00:18:28,387
-Toshiko, you've done so well.
-Toshiko!

186
00:18:28,488 --> 00:18:30,189
(SPEAKING JAPAN ESE)

187
00:18:32,159 --> 00:18:34,860
You've got what you want.
Now let her go.

188
00:18:34,961 --> 00:18:37,663
Well, except now,
you're the victim of your own success.

189
00:18:37,764 --> 00:18:42,935
Perfectly situated, proven ability.
You can give us so much more.

190
00:18:43,036 --> 00:18:45,571
(SPEAKING JAPAN ESE)

191
00:18:46,673 --> 00:18:50,142
-And what if I refuse?
-Then your mother stays with us.

192
00:18:50,944 --> 00:18:53,712
And your brilliance is used against her.

193
00:18:55,782 --> 00:18:57,783
-Like this.
-No. Don't...

194
00:18:57,884 --> 00:19:00,486
(SCREAMING)

195
00:19:21,708 --> 00:19:25,945
SOLDIER 1: Turn it off! Turn it off!
SOLDIER 2 : Get down !

196
00:19:29,482 --> 00:19:31,183
TOSHIKO: My mother!

197
00:19:32,285 --> 00:19:34,720
Is she all right? Is she all right?

198
00:19:47,767 --> 00:19:49,768
WOMAN ON SPEAKER:
This is a UNIT facility.

199
00:19:49,870 --> 00:19:52,605
Your rights as a citizen
have been withdrawn.

200
00:19:52,706 --> 00:19:54,607
You'll be held here indefinitely.

201
00:19:54,708 --> 00:19:58,377
We are not required to provide you
with legal representation.

202
00:19:58,478 --> 00:20:01,080
Anything you say will be recorded.

203
00:20:01,181 --> 00:20:05,751
You will be allowed no communication
with any person or organisation

204
00:20:05,852 --> 00:20:07,686
outside this facility.

205
00:20:07,787 --> 00:20:10,122
There is no right of appeal.

206
00:20:10,223 --> 00:20:14,727
If you fail to comply with the rules,
we are authorised to discipline you.

207
00:20:14,828 --> 00:20:15,928
Is my mother safe?

208
00:20:16,029 --> 00:20:18,864
We cannot supply you
with that information.

209
00:21:07,247 --> 00:21:09,315
Prisoner Sato, inspection.

210
00:21:11,051 --> 00:21:12,685
What for?

211
00:21:12,786 --> 00:21:14,720
Prepare for inspection.

212
00:21:25,999 --> 00:21:27,833
(DOOR U N LOCKING)

213
00:21:42,482 --> 00:21:45,317
JACK: Catering's as lousy
as they say, huh?

214
00:21:52,726 --> 00:21:54,693
-TOSHIKO: Where's my mother?
-She's safe.

215
00:21:54,794 --> 00:21:57,963
She won't remember being kidnapped.
I wiped it from her memory.

216
00:21:58,064 --> 00:22:00,599
-I hope you don't mind.
-You did what?

217
00:22:00,700 --> 00:22:02,768
Really just a little pill.

218
00:22:04,037 --> 00:22:06,005
She'll never have known.

219
00:22:06,706 --> 00:22:08,507
-Who are you?
-Nobody.

220
00:22:09,309 --> 00:22:10,809
I don't exist.

221
00:22:13,179 --> 00:22:16,949
And for a man with my charisma,
that's quite an achievement.

222
00:22:17,550 --> 00:22:20,419
-Are you a lawyer?
-Do I look like a lawyer?

223
00:22:23,723 --> 00:22:26,058
They're going to make an example of you.

224
00:22:26,159 --> 00:22:28,727
Stealing official secrets
in today's climate,

225
00:22:28,828 --> 00:22:31,830
they're going to keep you here
without charge.

226
00:22:34,968 --> 00:22:38,637
-Forever.
-They can't do...

227
00:22:38,738 --> 00:22:41,240
They're never going to release you.

228
00:22:43,643 --> 00:22:44,943
I'm sorry.

229
00:22:51,718 --> 00:22:53,519
You made this, right?

230
00:22:55,889 --> 00:22:58,724
-I just followed the plans.
-Yeah, kinda.

231
00:22:59,893 --> 00:23:04,196
But first, you had to grasp the concept
of what a sonic modulator does.

232
00:23:04,931 --> 00:23:07,066
Most people would struggle with that.

233
00:23:07,167 --> 00:23:08,700
And another thing,

234
00:23:08,802 --> 00:23:11,503
-the plans don't work.
-What?

235
00:23:12,272 --> 00:23:15,641
The technical plans you followed,
they were wrong.

236
00:23:15,742 --> 00:23:19,545
They had mistakes in them.
That's why the plans were shelved.

237
00:23:21,648 --> 00:23:24,283
But you, Toshiko Sato,

238
00:23:25,652 --> 00:23:29,021
you automatically fixed things
as you went along.

239
00:23:29,122 --> 00:23:31,156
What I'm trying to say is,

240
00:23:32,725 --> 00:23:34,927
oh, baby you're good.

241
00:23:35,795 --> 00:23:37,763
I mean, you're good now,

242
00:23:38,798 --> 00:23:42,000
imagine what you'd be like
with a little training.

243
00:23:47,107 --> 00:23:50,142
Shame you're going to be locked up
for so long.

244
00:23:51,211 --> 00:23:55,714
-You've got to get me out of here.
-If you

245
00:23:56,483 --> 00:23:59,751
-come work for me.
-Really?

246
00:23:59,853 --> 00:24:03,789
Give me five years,
I'll get them to wipe your record clean.

247
00:24:04,724 --> 00:24:06,758
They owe me a few favours.

248
00:24:10,330 --> 00:24:13,232
-What do you do?
-Protect people.

249
00:24:14,434 --> 00:24:18,670
At least that's what I'm aiming for.
It's kind of a work in progress.

250
00:24:19,305 --> 00:24:21,173
-What about my mother?
-Limited contact only,

251
00:24:21,274 --> 00:24:23,442
you can send her postcards.

252
00:24:25,678 --> 00:24:27,412
So what do you say?

253
00:24:31,551 --> 00:24:35,087
-Why would you trust me?
-Instinct.

254
00:24:38,625 --> 00:24:43,595
It's going to be dangerous.
Think you could bear a little danger?

255
00:24:43,963 --> 00:24:45,531
(SCREAMING)

256
00:24:45,632 --> 00:24:47,266
GWEN : Stop, stop, stop! Stop!

257
00:24:47,367 --> 00:24:50,402
-Tosh, Tosh, you okay?
-You're making it worse.

258
00:24:51,204 --> 00:24:55,440
It's pushing down even more.
I think I've broken my arm.

259
00:24:55,542 --> 00:24:56,608
-Gwen...
-Yeah?

260
00:24:56,709 --> 00:24:59,244
If this pillar shifts down even more,
it will crush me.

261
00:24:59,345 --> 00:25:01,346
It's no good, Gwen. We're going to need
more strength...

262
00:25:01,447 --> 00:25:03,815
Okay, look, Jack has gone
to find Owen and Ianto.

263
00:25:03,917 --> 00:25:06,685
You're going to be fine, darling,
all right? You're going to be fine.

264
00:25:06,786 --> 00:25:08,620
You've got to hurry, please.

265
00:25:08,721 --> 00:25:10,322
-Gwen, help Jack. I'll stay here.
-Are you sure?

266
00:25:10,423 --> 00:25:12,391
-Yeah.
-I'm going to come back for you.

267
00:25:12,492 --> 00:25:14,793
-You're going to be okay.
-TOSHIKO: Okay.

268
00:25:15,862 --> 00:25:18,730
Gwen, this could've been you,
couldn't it? If you hadn't been late.

269
00:25:18,831 --> 00:25:20,599
Rhys, I haven't got time
for this now, okay?

270
00:25:20,700 --> 00:25:23,502
I've got to go
and try and find the others.

271
00:25:34,047 --> 00:25:35,581
(SCREAMING)

272
00:25:42,789 --> 00:25:46,325
JACK: Ianto! Ianto!

273
00:25:50,530 --> 00:25:52,231
(GROWLING)

274
00:26:07,513 --> 00:26:09,147
(JACK SCREAMING)

275
00:26:16,990 --> 00:26:18,724
(IANTO GRU NTING)

276
00:26:35,608 --> 00:26:38,277
-Thanks.
-No. Thank you.

277
00:26:40,513 --> 00:26:43,382
-And you are?
-Jones.

278
00:26:44,584 --> 00:26:48,153
-Ianto Jones.
-N ice to meet you, Jones, Ianto Jones.

279
00:26:48,755 --> 00:26:50,589
Captain Jack Harkness.

280
00:26:51,124 --> 00:26:53,759
-Lucky escape.
-I had it under control.

281
00:26:54,160 --> 00:26:57,229
You think so? Looked pretty vicious.

282
00:26:59,599 --> 00:27:01,066
You're, um...

283
00:27:03,102 --> 00:27:06,305
-You were bleeding.
-Had worse from shaving.

284
00:27:08,241 --> 00:27:10,309
Looked like a Weevil to me.

285
00:27:10,910 --> 00:27:13,679
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

286
00:27:16,749 --> 00:27:18,750
I'll take him from here.

287
00:27:25,858 --> 00:27:29,328
-Thanks for the assistance.
-Any time.

288
00:27:32,398 --> 00:27:35,000
By the way, love the coat.

289
00:27:45,044 --> 00:27:46,278
Morning.

290
00:27:48,848 --> 00:27:50,048
Coffee?

291
00:27:59,826 --> 00:28:00,926
Wow.

292
00:28:01,761 --> 00:28:03,495
-I wanna work for you.
-Sorry. No vacancies.

293
00:28:03,596 --> 00:28:05,697
-Look, let me tell you about myself.
-Ianto Jones.

294
00:28:05,798 --> 00:28:10,202
Born August 19th, 1983.
Able student, but not exceptional.

295
00:28:10,303 --> 00:28:12,938
One minor conviction for shoplifting
in your teens.

296
00:28:13,039 --> 00:28:15,440
N umber of temporary jobs,
mainly a drifter,

297
00:28:15,541 --> 00:28:18,677
until two years ago, you joined
the Torchwood Institute in London.

298
00:28:18,778 --> 00:28:20,879
Junior researcher.
Girlfriend, Lisa Hallett.

299
00:28:20,980 --> 00:28:22,280
-Deceased.
-Sorry.

300
00:28:22,382 --> 00:28:27,386
-Look, you checked me out.
-You knew what a Weevil was.

301
00:28:27,487 --> 00:28:29,054
Thought I was going to have to come
"deal with you".

302
00:28:29,155 --> 00:28:31,423
But instead, you can see I have
the right qualifications for the job.

303
00:28:31,524 --> 00:28:35,127
There is no job. We're nothing to do
with Torchwood London.

304
00:28:35,228 --> 00:28:37,028
I severed all links.

305
00:28:37,130 --> 00:28:40,899
Yet when it burnt, two members
of your team scavenged the ruins.

306
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:43,402
I don't want the equipment
getting into the wrong hands.

307
00:28:43,503 --> 00:28:45,570
And you're the right hands, are you?

308
00:28:45,671 --> 00:28:47,606
-Trial period. Three months.
-No.

309
00:28:47,707 --> 00:28:50,008
Three weeks. Three days.

310
00:28:50,109 --> 00:28:51,810
Let me prove myself to you.
I'll work for nothing.

311
00:28:51,878 --> 00:28:52,911
No.

312
00:28:53,846 --> 00:28:56,348
I saw what they did at Canary Wharf.

313
00:28:57,250 --> 00:28:58,817
What am I supposed to do
with those memories?

314
00:28:58,918 --> 00:29:02,721
You are not my responsibility
and we're not hiring.

315
00:29:04,590 --> 00:29:06,124
Same time tomorrow, then.

316
00:29:06,225 --> 00:29:09,594
There is no job for you here
and there never will be.

317
00:29:10,263 --> 00:29:12,230
I really like that coat.

318
00:29:15,435 --> 00:29:17,903
JACK ON RADIO: Toshiko, see if you can
decode those hieroglyphics.

319
00:29:18,004 --> 00:29:19,337
TOSHIKO: Already on it.

320
00:29:19,439 --> 00:29:21,273
JACK: Owen, take a cross-section
of the paramedic's brain.

321
00:29:21,374 --> 00:29:22,741
Check it against
the list of chemical agents.

322
00:29:22,842 --> 00:29:23,909
OWEN : Will do.

323
00:29:24,010 --> 00:29:26,044
JACK: Suzie, we're going to need
to dredge the reservoir.

324
00:29:26,145 --> 00:29:28,647
See if you can find the other half...

325
00:29:29,348 --> 00:29:30,382
Oh.

326
00:29:32,919 --> 00:29:34,953
-Okay, this has to stop.
-No. Listen to me.

327
00:29:35,054 --> 00:29:39,291
I don't have time for this.
Look, I don't care what your problem is.

328
00:29:39,392 --> 00:29:42,661
I want you out of this city by sunrise.
There is no place for you here.

329
00:29:42,762 --> 00:29:44,763
Go back to London,
find yourself another life.

330
00:29:44,864 --> 00:29:46,665
Keep stalking me, I'll wipe your memory.

331
00:29:46,766 --> 00:29:49,134
-No, but the thing is...
-Look, any conversation between us,

332
00:29:49,235 --> 00:29:52,804
no matter what the subject, is over.
Finished. Done. Forever.

333
00:29:53,306 --> 00:29:54,940
I'm getting back
behind the wheel of that car,

334
00:29:55,041 --> 00:29:58,844
if you're still standing in the road,
I'm gonna drive through you.

335
00:29:58,945 --> 00:30:02,681
So you're not going to help me
catch this pterodactyl, then?

336
00:30:04,784 --> 00:30:07,219
Okay, that is the only
special equipment you've got?

337
00:30:07,320 --> 00:30:10,222
Yeah. 'Cause I keep dinosaur nuts
in the back of the SUV.

338
00:30:10,323 --> 00:30:12,357
Torchwood London would've...

339
00:30:18,498 --> 00:30:20,465
(PTERODACTYL SQUAWKING)

340
00:30:20,566 --> 00:30:21,666
Nope.

341
00:30:24,136 --> 00:30:26,471
-How did you find it?
-Rift Activity Locator.

342
00:30:26,572 --> 00:30:28,540
-Torchwood London.
-See, quality kit.

343
00:30:28,641 --> 00:30:32,110
-Yeah, it's quite excitable.
-Must be the aftershave.

344
00:30:32,211 --> 00:30:34,312
-Never wear any.
-You smell like that naturally?

345
00:30:34,413 --> 00:30:38,250
5 1 st century pheromones.
People have no idea.

346
00:30:39,619 --> 00:30:41,286
-Ready for another go?
-I'm game if you are.

347
00:30:41,387 --> 00:30:43,154
Three, two, one.

348
00:30:45,992 --> 00:30:47,959
(PTERODACTYL SQUAWKING)

349
00:30:51,297 --> 00:30:52,898
Shh. Shh. Shh.

350
00:30:53,933 --> 00:30:55,567
(JACK CH UCKLING)

351
00:30:56,802 --> 00:31:00,138
We're not going to harm you.
You can't stay here.

352
00:31:01,040 --> 00:31:02,941
Come back with me.

353
00:31:03,042 --> 00:31:06,077
I've got somewhere nice and big
where you can fly around.

354
00:31:06,178 --> 00:31:08,280
Okay, so you let the pterodactyl in
but not me?

355
00:31:08,381 --> 00:31:11,316
-I need a guard dog.
-I could be that.

356
00:31:11,417 --> 00:31:14,986
A receptionist? Building maintenance?

357
00:31:15,087 --> 00:31:16,588
Food and drink?

358
00:31:17,390 --> 00:31:20,492
Dry cleaning even? That coat of yours
must take a battering.

359
00:31:20,593 --> 00:31:22,894
-Like a butler, I could be a butler.
-We don't need a butler.

360
00:31:22,995 --> 00:31:25,230
Excuse me. Dried egg on your collar.

361
00:31:25,331 --> 00:31:28,433
-It was a busy week.
-What exactly is your plan?

362
00:31:29,735 --> 00:31:32,971
-I'm gonna be the decoy.
-And it won't rip you to shreds?

363
00:31:33,072 --> 00:31:37,142
Dinosaurs? Had them for breakfast.
Had to.

364
00:31:37,243 --> 00:31:40,779
Only source of food protein
after the asteroid crashed.

365
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:42,881
Long story. Here you go.

366
00:31:44,216 --> 00:31:46,785
One injection to
the central nervous cortex.

367
00:31:46,886 --> 00:31:49,020
I'll keep it occupied. Move.

368
00:31:49,121 --> 00:31:50,589
-No.
-What?

369
00:31:50,690 --> 00:31:53,024
It knows me. I'll be a better decoy.

370
00:31:53,125 --> 00:31:55,694
-Way too dangerous.
-No, I've got a secret weapon.

371
00:31:55,795 --> 00:31:57,896
Chocolate. Preferably dark.

372
00:32:01,834 --> 00:32:03,501
(WHISTLING)

373
00:32:07,006 --> 00:32:09,007
Got your favourite. Yeah.

374
00:32:10,009 --> 00:32:11,977
(PTERODACTYL SCREECHING)

375
00:32:19,986 --> 00:32:23,221
It's good for your serotonin levels,

376
00:32:23,322 --> 00:32:26,524
if you've got serotonin levels.

377
00:32:31,063 --> 00:32:32,163
Whoa !

378
00:32:33,265 --> 00:32:35,100
Whoa ! Ianto!

379
00:32:43,442 --> 00:32:45,010
(JACK GRU NTING)

380
00:32:52,885 --> 00:32:54,052
Sorry.

381
00:32:57,089 --> 00:32:58,690
(BOTH LAUGHING)

382
00:33:06,799 --> 00:33:08,199
I should go.

383
00:33:15,608 --> 00:33:16,708
Hey!

384
00:33:17,143 --> 00:33:19,744
Report for work first thing tomorrow.

385
00:33:25,484 --> 00:33:27,485
Like the suit by the way.

386
00:33:31,824 --> 00:33:33,358
(JACK GRU NTING)

387
00:33:34,560 --> 00:33:37,962
JACK: Ready? Three.
One, two, three. Come on.

388
00:33:38,064 --> 00:33:41,466
Oh, my God. Come on. Come on, come on.

389
00:33:41,567 --> 00:33:43,334
(IANTO SCREAMING)

390
00:33:43,969 --> 00:33:47,472
-You okay?
-My shoulder. I think it's dislocated.

391
00:33:47,573 --> 00:33:49,274
-Can you take this?
-Yeah.

392
00:33:49,375 --> 00:33:51,109
Take a deep breath.

393
00:33:57,383 --> 00:33:59,517
-Where are the others?
-We need your help to get Toshiko out.

394
00:33:59,618 --> 00:34:01,386
-Owen?
-No sign yet.

395
00:34:01,487 --> 00:34:03,054
If anything happens,
he can't repair himself.

396
00:34:03,155 --> 00:34:06,491
-Of course, he can't heal, can he?
-Okay, we'll help Rhys with Toshiko.

397
00:34:06,592 --> 00:34:08,727
Let us know when you find Owen,
and be careful.

398
00:34:08,828 --> 00:34:09,928
Okay.

399
00:34:10,930 --> 00:34:12,630
Okay? You all right?

400
00:34:13,833 --> 00:34:15,133
(CREAKING)

401
00:34:38,023 --> 00:34:40,391
Oh, go on.
Please, please, please, please.

402
00:34:40,493 --> 00:34:41,793
No. You don't even like her,

403
00:34:41,894 --> 00:34:44,129
ever since she didn't pay for her share
of the Chinese in Leicester.

404
00:34:44,230 --> 00:34:45,396
Yeah, but we want Julia to come

405
00:34:45,498 --> 00:34:47,165
and it'd look odd
if we invite one without the other.

406
00:34:47,266 --> 00:34:49,868
Oh, God, help me please. Help me, God.

407
00:34:50,469 --> 00:34:52,937
Three tables done. N ine more to go.

408
00:34:53,773 --> 00:34:57,008
You wanna back out?
It's still not too late.

409
00:34:58,577 --> 00:35:00,979
Listen, I'm marrying you

410
00:35:01,847 --> 00:35:04,249
even if it kills me, okay?

411
00:35:04,350 --> 00:35:05,617
H mm.

412
00:35:10,055 --> 00:35:11,189
Good.

413
00:35:12,792 --> 00:35:14,626
You want a cup of tea?

414
00:35:15,895 --> 00:35:19,063
-Yeah, I'll make one.
-Think I can manage.

415
00:35:29,608 --> 00:35:31,342
-Katie?
-Yeah?

416
00:35:33,746 --> 00:35:35,313
Erm...

417
00:35:35,381 --> 00:35:36,781
Water.

418
00:35:37,583 --> 00:35:38,950
Yeah.

419
00:35:40,986 --> 00:35:42,587
From the kettle.

420
00:35:45,624 --> 00:35:47,192
(KATIE SIGHING)

421
00:35:54,533 --> 00:35:55,633
Milk.

422
00:35:55,734 --> 00:35:57,869
Stop nagging me.
I don't want to have milk.

423
00:35:57,970 --> 00:36:00,505
I've never liked milk. I want to have...

424
00:36:03,342 --> 00:36:06,377
-Tea.
-I wanna have tea without...

425
00:36:06,478 --> 00:36:07,812
(SIGHING)

426
00:36:09,949 --> 00:36:12,150
-Milk.
-Tea without milk.

427
00:36:15,354 --> 00:36:16,955
(BANGING)

428
00:36:19,391 --> 00:36:20,658
(KATIE CRYING)

429
00:36:20,759 --> 00:36:22,894
It's all right. It's all right.

430
00:36:26,098 --> 00:36:29,868
MAN : I got your invitation.
It's still going ahead?

431
00:36:30,469 --> 00:36:33,738
-I promised her a summer wedding.
-Before all this.

432
00:36:34,273 --> 00:36:37,775
-This changes nothing.
-Owen, it will change everything.

433
00:36:39,545 --> 00:36:42,580
-You don't know for certain.
-We've been through Kate's test results

434
00:36:42,681 --> 00:36:45,083
more times than any patient
in my whole career.

435
00:36:45,184 --> 00:36:47,151
You've looked through them yourself.

436
00:36:47,253 --> 00:36:50,655
All the evidence suggests
she has early onset Alzheimer's.

437
00:36:50,756 --> 00:36:54,592
-The youngest case in medical history.
-Doesn't mean we're wrong.

438
00:36:54,660 --> 00:36:56,094
OWEN : Please.

439
00:36:56,795 --> 00:37:00,164
Run more tests.
Let's just try one more MRI scan.

440
00:37:00,266 --> 00:37:02,834
-An MRI isn't gonna make any difference.
-You don't know that now.

441
00:37:02,935 --> 00:37:06,204
You have said yourself that this
is unlike any case that you've seen.

442
00:37:06,305 --> 00:37:08,039
-Maybe you've missed something.
-Owen.

443
00:37:08,140 --> 00:37:10,642
You don't understand, Jim, okay?

444
00:37:10,743 --> 00:37:13,378
One day she's fine,
she has perfect memory, the old Katie,

445
00:37:13,479 --> 00:37:16,214
and the next, there's nothing.
She's blank.

446
00:37:16,315 --> 00:37:18,249
Now I am losing her

447
00:37:18,350 --> 00:37:20,785
and I don't know
what to do about that, okay?

448
00:37:20,853 --> 00:37:22,186
So please...

449
00:37:23,789 --> 00:37:28,159
What's the point of me doing this job
if I can't help my own fiancée?

450
00:37:28,260 --> 00:37:31,796
-I'll see what I can do.
-Thank you, Jim.

451
00:38:22,314 --> 00:38:23,581
It's like

452
00:38:24,783 --> 00:38:28,886
being lost in a place you know really
well, you can't get your bearings.

453
00:38:28,988 --> 00:38:32,023
Sometimes it comes back to you
and sometimes...

454
00:38:33,225 --> 00:38:34,826
I'm sorry, Owen.

455
00:38:35,594 --> 00:38:37,895
What've you got to be sorry for?

456
00:38:39,465 --> 00:38:42,066
I don't want to put you through this.

457
00:38:43,869 --> 00:38:46,504
Last night, I dreamt that you left me.

458
00:38:47,139 --> 00:38:50,441
Come on. Nobody's leaving anyone.

459
00:38:52,444 --> 00:38:54,078
(KATIE SNIFFLING)

460
00:38:58,283 --> 00:38:59,717
How is that possible?

461
00:38:59,818 --> 00:39:02,854
We don't know.
I've never seen anything like it.

462
00:39:02,955 --> 00:39:06,324
It's not the brain deteriorating,
it's a clear physical tumour.

463
00:39:06,425 --> 00:39:09,460
-That wasn't there last week?
-Not that we saw.

464
00:39:10,829 --> 00:39:15,733
-You were right to ask for another scan.
-So, what do we do now?

465
00:39:15,834 --> 00:39:17,969
We have to view this as good news.

466
00:39:18,070 --> 00:39:22,840
Katie, we need to take you into surgery
soon as possible and remove the tumour.

467
00:39:24,476 --> 00:39:25,977
You understand?

468
00:39:27,713 --> 00:39:28,880
Katie?

469
00:39:30,416 --> 00:39:32,517
I can't remember your name.

470
00:39:41,026 --> 00:39:42,627
You sure she's up to this?

471
00:39:42,728 --> 00:39:45,596
We're going to do everything
we can for her.

472
00:40:09,521 --> 00:40:11,856
-I'm sorry.
-Who the hell are you?

473
00:40:11,957 --> 00:40:13,925
I tried to tell them
you should prepare for the worst.

474
00:40:14,026 --> 00:40:16,060
No, you can't go in there.

475
00:40:22,067 --> 00:40:23,634
Oh, my God.

476
00:40:25,237 --> 00:40:26,404
Katie.

477
00:40:31,610 --> 00:40:34,779
-What is it?
-I'm sorry, I tried to stop them.

478
00:40:35,747 --> 00:40:37,115
She's dead.

479
00:40:39,818 --> 00:40:42,787
That thing in her head
is an alien life form.

480
00:40:43,489 --> 00:40:47,391
It incubates in the brain,
disrupting the shape and functions.

481
00:40:48,627 --> 00:40:50,161
When it's attacked or threatened,

482
00:40:50,262 --> 00:40:52,864
it emits a toxic gas
that's fatal to humans.

483
00:40:52,965 --> 00:40:57,401
-It clears pretty quickly.
-She can't be dead. She can't be dead.

484
00:40:57,503 --> 00:40:58,703
I'm calling the police.

485
00:40:58,804 --> 00:41:01,439
Tell them that Torchwood's
already here and dealing with it.

486
00:41:01,540 --> 00:41:05,843
That'll save them a call-out.
I need to take her brain back with me.

487
00:41:05,944 --> 00:41:08,346
Don't touch her. Don't touch her.

488
00:41:25,931 --> 00:41:27,465
-How are you feeling?
-Where is she?

489
00:41:27,566 --> 00:41:29,367
-Where is who?
-Katie. Katie Russell.

490
00:41:29,468 --> 00:41:31,736
She's a junior doctor. She works here
and we're about to get married.

491
00:41:31,837 --> 00:41:35,406
-Let's get you back into bed.
-Get off me! Where is she?

492
00:41:36,275 --> 00:41:38,943
(SHOUTING) Where is she? Where is she?

493
00:41:40,212 --> 00:41:44,482
He was wearing a military uniform.
He has an American accent.

494
00:41:45,150 --> 00:41:47,985
I promise, we have checked
all the security footage.

495
00:41:48,086 --> 00:41:49,220
There was no such man.

496
00:41:49,321 --> 00:41:52,623
Jim Garrett was poisoned
by some alien toxin.

497
00:41:52,724 --> 00:41:54,525
Jim Garrett was in a car accident.

498
00:41:54,626 --> 00:41:57,562
The American said that
he wanted her brain and there was...

499
00:41:57,663 --> 00:41:59,931
There was an alien creature or...

500
00:42:01,500 --> 00:42:04,569
This happened, okay?
This is not some trauma

501
00:42:04,670 --> 00:42:08,005
or delayed grief
or whatever you're scribbling down.

502
00:42:09,474 --> 00:42:11,509
Katie's tumour was inoperable.

503
00:42:11,610 --> 00:42:13,644
There was nothing
anyone could have done.

504
00:42:13,745 --> 00:42:16,948
This is just... This is wrong.

505
00:42:17,316 --> 00:42:20,017
I'm giving you three months'
prescribed rest.

506
00:42:20,118 --> 00:42:23,588
-Don't come into work.
-Yeah.

507
00:42:30,262 --> 00:42:33,331
This isn't right. He was there.

508
00:42:36,268 --> 00:42:39,237
It wasn't just me. He was there, too.

509
00:42:40,672 --> 00:42:43,174
That is not what happened.

510
00:42:43,275 --> 00:42:45,843
That's not what happened.

511
00:43:25,684 --> 00:43:26,917
You !

512
00:43:32,324 --> 00:43:35,359
You could have saved her!
You could have saved her!

513
00:43:36,561 --> 00:43:39,397
You could have...
You could have saved her.

514
00:43:44,569 --> 00:43:47,138
I couldn't. I really couldn't.

515
00:43:47,239 --> 00:43:49,006
(OWEN CRYING)

516
00:43:55,914 --> 00:43:58,816
OWEN : You're not a figment
of my imagination

517
00:43:58,917 --> 00:44:00,685
and I don't know
what's happening any more.

518
00:44:00,786 --> 00:44:03,954
Maybe this is
what a mental breakdown feels like.

519
00:44:05,090 --> 00:44:06,390
JACK: You're fine.

520
00:44:06,491 --> 00:44:09,427
It's the rest of the world
that's delusional.

521
00:44:10,829 --> 00:44:12,063
Why her?

522
00:44:13,532 --> 00:44:15,232
There is no reason.

523
00:44:16,435 --> 00:44:18,736
Your life doesn't end with her.

524
00:44:20,205 --> 00:44:21,739
What are you going to do now?

525
00:44:21,840 --> 00:44:25,209
Go back to work?
See echoes of her in every corridor?

526
00:44:25,310 --> 00:44:28,145
You need a purpose.
I'm building something.

527
00:44:28,947 --> 00:44:32,683
-I need a medic.
-You want me?

528
00:44:33,518 --> 00:44:37,288
You made them take more scans,
kept trying to track me down.

529
00:44:37,989 --> 00:44:39,490
You don't give up easily.

530
00:44:39,591 --> 00:44:42,526
I need someone like that
to work with me in Cardiff.

531
00:44:42,627 --> 00:44:45,196
-To fight aliens?
-Exactly.

532
00:44:47,466 --> 00:44:51,369
Look, I...
I don't know what happened to Katie.

533
00:44:52,137 --> 00:44:54,638
And I don't know who you really are.

534
00:44:54,906 --> 00:44:58,242
-But there is no such thing as aliens.
-You think?

535
00:45:01,113 --> 00:45:05,549
I'm having a breakdown,
a mental collapse.

536
00:45:09,521 --> 00:45:10,654
Owen.

537
00:45:11,723 --> 00:45:13,891
Why did you become a doctor?

538
00:45:15,026 --> 00:45:19,230
I thought if I could save one life,
mine would be worthwhile.

539
00:45:21,166 --> 00:45:24,368
But you save one,
and there's another and another

540
00:45:25,470 --> 00:45:28,105
clawing at you, demanding to be saved.

541
00:45:29,641 --> 00:45:34,044
And even if you do succeed,
you can never save enough.

542
00:45:37,716 --> 00:45:39,450
Maybe here you can.

543
00:45:46,391 --> 00:45:47,858
-Heavens.
-H i.

544
00:45:47,926 --> 00:45:49,794
Careful!

545
00:45:49,895 --> 00:45:52,163
-If that falls...
-Okay, softly.

546
00:45:53,698 --> 00:45:55,199
(BOTH SCREAM)

547
00:45:56,334 --> 00:45:57,868
-Okay.
-Just be very careful.

548
00:45:57,969 --> 00:46:00,671
Okay, all right. I'm gonna get you out.

549
00:46:00,772 --> 00:46:03,374
This one. Okay.

550
00:46:03,475 --> 00:46:05,910
-You have do it very, very gently.
-Okay.

551
00:46:06,011 --> 00:46:08,045
There's no way
this is gonna drop on you.

552
00:46:08,113 --> 00:46:09,680
Whoa !

553
00:46:10,148 --> 00:46:12,316
-Quiet.
-Okay. Okay, silent.

554
00:46:12,417 --> 00:46:14,452
I'm going to do this
as quickly as possible.

555
00:46:14,553 --> 00:46:16,220
Listen to me,
I'm going to get you out of this.

556
00:46:16,321 --> 00:46:18,055
Look at me. Trust me.

557
00:46:18,156 --> 00:46:19,957
-Okay, Owen, hold my hand.
-Slowly.

558
00:46:20,058 --> 00:46:21,592
Hold my hands.

559
00:46:26,097 --> 00:46:28,699
JACK: You okay?
OWEN : Yeah.

560
00:46:28,800 --> 00:46:31,101
You all right? Tosh, what happened?

561
00:46:31,203 --> 00:46:33,170
TOSHIKO: Broken arm. Bruised ribs.

562
00:46:33,271 --> 00:46:36,173
About an inch away
from being crushed by a girder.

563
00:46:36,274 --> 00:46:38,142
OWEN : We were lucky.
IANTO: We all were.

564
00:46:38,243 --> 00:46:39,977
-Jack, who's done this?
-I don't...

565
00:46:40,078 --> 00:46:41,912
RHYS: Where's the SUV?

566
00:46:42,781 --> 00:46:44,048
(BEEPING)

567
00:46:44,149 --> 00:46:46,350
-Oh, no.
-Jack, what does he want?

568
00:46:46,451 --> 00:46:51,288
Oh, déjà vu. Or did I say that already?
Hey, team!

569
00:46:51,389 --> 00:46:54,825
Of course, there might be
a few less of you by now.

570
00:46:54,926 --> 00:46:59,597
Don't know if you liked my little gift.
Of course, you can't die.

571
00:47:01,132 --> 00:47:04,535
And with all that life, all that time,

572
00:47:04,636 --> 00:47:07,338
you can't spare any for me. Oh!

573
00:47:08,440 --> 00:47:10,374
Say hi to the family.

574
00:47:12,177 --> 00:47:13,377
No way. It can't be.

575
00:47:13,478 --> 00:47:16,914
Been a while since
you've seen your brother, eh, Jack?

576
00:47:17,716 --> 00:47:18,849
Gray?

577
00:47:19,451 --> 00:47:22,019
Okay, here is what's going to happen.

578
00:47:22,120 --> 00:47:25,556
Everything you love,
everything you treasure, will die.

579
00:47:26,258 --> 00:47:28,759
I'm going to tear your world apart,

580
00:47:29,494 --> 00:47:31,328
Captain Jack Harkness.

581
00:47:31,796 --> 00:47:34,031
Piece by piece. Starting now.

582
00:47:35,300 --> 00:47:38,302
Maybe now you'll want
to spend some time with me.

583
00:47:46,778 --> 00:47:48,546
This was a targeted attack.

584
00:47:48,647 --> 00:47:51,181
He killed the four most senior officers.

585
00:47:51,283 --> 00:47:54,184
If it gets out what happened here,
there'll be a city-wide panic.

586
00:47:54,286 --> 00:47:56,120
Let's go get ourselves a good view.

587
00:47:56,721 --> 00:47:58,022
What have you done?

588
00:47:58,123 --> 00:47:59,857
We're going to put
this city back together.

589
00:47:59,958 --> 00:48:01,992
We're going to find Jack.

590
00:48:02,093 --> 00:48:03,761
And we're going to punish John.

591
00:48:03,862 --> 00:48:05,863
He's completely crippled us, Gwen.

592
00:48:05,931 --> 00:48:07,264
You're no fun.

593
00:48:07,365 --> 00:48:08,799
Owen, get out of there.

594
00:48:09,301 --> 00:48:10,668
What have you done with my brother?

595
00:48:10,769 --> 00:48:13,170
This is going to get nasty.

596
00:48:14,573 --> 00:48:16,273
What if this is how it all ends?
